<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise data-content-id="9f003b7b-c462-41fb-9132-5dfd019c4547" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Based on your work above, which of the six equations are equivalent to the original equation, \(x−0.1x+2.70=56.70\)? Select the <emphasis>three</emphasis> equations that are equivalent to the original.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Compare your answer: A, B, C were all equivalent equations to the original with 60 as a solution.</para><para>Nice try! The correct answers are \(100x-10x+270=5670\), \(x-0.1x=54\), and \(0.9x+2.70=56.70\). </para></solution></exercise></section><title>Video: Looking at Equivalent Equations</title>
